# Lines tools/pi-run must see, in this order, as whole serial lines (the Pi
# 5 only: rpi5b_2gb/run-length-test.system). The watchdog PD,
# watching no PD, arms the PM watchdog at each of the ticker's ticks until
# the run length, 60 s; then the ticker stops, and the PM watchdog resets
# the board (pi-run waits for it, and parks the board at U-Boot's prompt).
NOWAYOS: watchdog: the PM watchdog, armed for 6 s at each servicing
NOWAYOS: watchdog: watching no PD: the PM watchdog is serviced on every tick, for 6 s, for as long as the ticks come
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: ticker: a tick to the watchdog every 2000 ms for the run length, 60 s
NOWAYOS: watchdog: first tick: hardware watchdog serviced
NOWAYOS: watchdog-stand-in: ticker: the run length is reached: no more ticks, so the watchdog services no more and the board resets

# Output that fails the run at once if it appears anywhere (substring match).
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!gave up
!could not service
!not 1 to
!panicked
